speechtext:
Oh, yes, with pleasure; and it is very simple when you know how it is done. Collectors do not have to pass the civil service examination, nor preventive officers, nor landing waiters.
123}
Appraisers have to pass special examinations. As I have explained before, I recognize the spirit of the Act to be that we should endeavour to get as many as we can to pass the qualifying examination, but in certain cases we take advantage of the clause allowing us to appoint clerks to the position of preventive officer without their undergoing examination. Where there are employees who have been years in the service and who are faithful and competent officers, but who do not feel competent to pass the qualifying examinations, we put them on as preventive officers. It would be very difficult for men who have been on the staff for years to pass this literary examination-I doubt whether I could pass it myself -and it would not be fair to compel them to do so.
